// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/cache-and-security-headers.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeCacheAndSecurityHeaders(path: "/recipes/cache-and-security-headers", title: "Set cache and security headers — Recipes", description: "Which Cache-Control each file of a WebFluent build should get, and the security headers the build writes to _headers for a host to send.") {
    RecipeShell("Set cache and security headers", summary: "This recipe sets the HTTP headers a host sends with a WebFluent build: how long a browser may keep each file, and the security headers that only work as real headers.  You need a host that lets you set headers, or one that reads `_headers` (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages). The hosting recipes, such as [Serve a site with nginx](/recipes/serve-with-nginx), show where each host takes them.  With `build.csp` on, this is the `build/_headers` file a build writes:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "set-cache-headers", label: "Set cache headers"), Anchor(id: "set-security-headers", label: "Set security headers")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Install wf on a build machine", to: "/recipes/install-wf-in-ci"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Use environment values, and keep secrets out", to: "/recipes/environments-and-secrets"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to GitHub Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-github-pages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/cache-and-security-headers.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            CodeBlock(#"/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY"#, title: "text")
        }
        Markdown("1. `/*` applies the headers under it to every path of the site.\n2. `Content-Security-Policy` is the same policy every page already carries as a `<meta>` tag, plus `frame-ancestors`, which a browser ignores in a `<meta>` tag ([Security](/about/security#ship-a-content-security-policy)).\n3. `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy` and `X-Frame-Options` only work as real HTTP headers, so they are in this file and nowhere else.\n\nThe build writes no cache headers: those are yours to set, by the kind of file.")

        Heading("Set cache headers", id: "set-cache-headers").h2

        Markdown("To let browsers keep files without serving a stale site, set `Cache-Control` by the kind of file:")

        Table(caption: "Set cache headers") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Files").header
                    Table.Cell("Cache-Control").header
                    Table.Cell("Why").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("HTML, `app.js`, `pages/*`, `styles.css`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`no-cache` (revalidate every time)") }
                    Table.Cell("their names do not change between builds")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`sw.js`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`no-cache`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("a stale worker holds a stale site ([Make a site work offline](/recipes/work-offline))") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("resized images (`hero.<hash>.960.webp`)") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`public, max-age=31536000, immutable`") }
                    Table.Cell("the name changes when the file does")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`public/` files") }
                    Table.Cell("your choice")
                    Table.Cell("they keep the names you gave them")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("`no-cache` still lets the browser keep a copy. The browser asks the server each time, and a `304 Not Modified` answer means it does not download the file again.")

        Heading("Set security headers", id: "set-security-headers").h2

        Markdown("Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read `build/_headers` as it is. On any other host, set the same headers in its configuration, as the hosting recipes show: [nginx](/recipes/serve-with-nginx), [Apache](/recipes/serve-with-apache), [Caddy](/recipes/serve-with-caddy) and [Vercel](/recipes/deploy-to-vercel). Serve the site over HTTPS, and turn on HSTS once you are sure HTTPS works everywhere. [Security](/about/security#before-you-deploy) has the full checklist.\n\nAfter the deploy, [check the headers it sends](/recipes/check-a-deploy).")

    }
}
